# Three-position switch, for an aircraft whose COMPASS IS NOT YET CALIBRATED.
#
# Same as 51-fltmodes-3pos but with LAND in place of RTL.
#
# Why: RTL needs a trustworthy heading and position. It flies a compass bearing
# home. With an uncalibrated compass -- offsets still belonging to the internal
# sensor, orientation never verified -- RTL will confidently fly the wrong way,
# and it does that at altitude, away from you, with no warning.
#
# LAND needs neither. It descends where it is, on the barometer alone. It is a
# genuine recovery mode with none of the dependencies, which makes it the right
# thing to have on the switch until the compass work is done.
#
#   slot 1  STABILIZE  manual
#   slot 4  ALT_HOLD   holds height
#   slot 6  LAND       put it down, here, now
#
# After the compass is calibrated and verified outdoors, switch to
# 51-fltmodes-3pos to get RTL back.
FLTMODE1 0
FLTMODE2 0
FLTMODE3 2
FLTMODE4 2
FLTMODE5 9
FLTMODE6 9
